1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
A Taiwan website offer. From one hundred
ninety-nine New Taiwan dollars.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,167
Mobile layout, a form, deployment,
unlimited revisions.

3
00:00:09,167 --> 00:00:14,633
The quote is simpler. One static page.
Client-provided content. One revision.

4
00:00:14,633 --> 00:00:18,267
Service Requirement Blueprint makes the
gap visible.

5
00:00:18,267 --> 00:00:22,992
The client writes down what they need.
JSON A freezes that baseline.

6
00:00:22,992 --> 00:00:26,467
It records the workflow, deliverables, and
budget.

7
00:00:26,467 --> 00:00:29,449
This scene illustrates the negotiation.

8
00:00:29,449 --> 00:00:35,338
The client asks for the form and mobile
button. The contractor includes both.

9
00:00:35,338 --> 00:00:39,392
Deployment stays excluded. So do unlimited
revisions.

10
00:00:39,392 --> 00:00:42,833
They agree on the checks before
confirmation.

11
00:00:42,833 --> 00:00:49,500
Now the actual case record. Both parties'
messages stay in the case record.

12
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:54,544
JSON B states the revised offer. The form
and mobile button are included.

13
00:00:54,544 --> 00:00:57,929
Deployment and unlimited revisions stay
excluded.

14
00:00:57,929 --> 00:01:00,900
The fee and acceptance checks are
explicit.

15
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:06,367
Test the form. Check the button at three
hundred ninety pixels.

16
00:01:06,367 --> 00:01:12,028
The client asks. The contractor answers.
The client accepts the revised scope.

17
00:01:12,028 --> 00:01:14,133
The issue is marked resolved.

18
00:01:14,133 --> 00:01:18,667
One party has confirmed. The other is
still pending.

19
00:01:18,667 --> 00:01:21,448
Both parties confirm the same version.

20
00:01:21,448 --> 00:01:25,033
That fixed version becomes their shared
baseline.

21
00:01:25,033 --> 00:01:30,500
The shared PDF preserves that version and
its workflow diagram.

22
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:36,838
The PDF also records scope, exclusions,
fees, and acceptance checks.

23
00:01:36,838 --> 00:01:40,100
Silence never counts as acceptance.

24
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:44,581
The form passes. The mobile button fails
the agreed check.

25
00:01:44,581 --> 00:01:48,367
The client records why and requests a
correction.

26
00:01:48,367 --> 00:01:50,151
This is a demonstration record.

27
00:01:50,151 --> 00:01:53,833
The contractor documents the correction
and supporting evidence.

28
00:01:53,833 --> 00:01:58,367
Resubmission starts a new inspection. The
earlier return stays in history.

29
00:01:58,367 --> 00:02:02,633
The client checks both items again. Both
pass.

30
00:02:02,633 --> 00:02:06,621
The client explicitly accepts the
delivery.

31
00:02:06,621 --> 00:02:12,000
Nothing is approved automatically. Silence
does not count.

32
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,851
The record keeps the full sequence. The
failure. The correction.

33
00:02:16,851 --> 00:02:18,367
The accepted result.

34
00:02:18,367 --> 00:02:22,733
Either party can export the same evidence
package.

35
00:02:22,733 --> 00:02:26,951
Here are the verified downloads. A shared
PDF. Version records.

36
00:02:26,951 --> 00:02:30,900
Delivery and inspection evidence. All
preserved in one ZIP.

37
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:34,775
The timeline links the delivery, return,
and correction.

38
00:02:34,775 --> 00:02:37,267
It also records explicit acceptance.

39
00:02:37,267 --> 00:02:41,800
The platform preserves evidence. It does
not decide who's right.
